	)
	(text "POWER SUPPLY SEQUENCE AS PER THE STM32MP135 DATASHEET IS\nVDD (3.3V) FOLLOWED BY VDD_DDR (1.35V), VDDCPU (1.25V),\nVDDCORE (1.25V). DURING THE BOOT PROCESS, CLOCK SPEED IS\nINCREASED FROM 650 MHZ TO 1 GHZ AND VDDCPU INCREASED TO\n1.35V. IN STOP MODE, VDDCORE IS REDUCED TO 0.9V. WHEN\nVDDA1V8_REG COMES UP, VDD_USB (3.3V) IS SWITCHED ON.\n\nTHE POWER SEQUENCE CAN BE SIMPLIFIED. WE DO NOT NEED THE STOP\nMODE, SO VDCORE CAN BE ALWAYS RUNNING AT 1.25V. VDDCPU CAN BE\nALWAYS SET TO 1.35V. THIS REDUCES LIFETIME WHEN OPERATING AT\nHIGH TEMPERATURES (>85C), BUT WE CAN MONITOR THE TEMPERATURE\nAND MAKE SURE THE INSTRUMENT DOES NOT GET TOO HOT. FINALLY,\nTHE USB SUPPLY IS SWITCHED ON (BY U105) ONCE THE 1.8V INTERNAL\nREGULATOR GETS TURNED ON."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 340.614 26.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9d07d1f6-2fb7-4311-9734-1925aecb46db")
	)
	(text "POWER SEQUENCE"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 340.106 20.066 0)
		(effects
